From 94004db83b6f15cfc7d29405e1ea0263e9e393c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 03:14:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(tokens): embedded-webfont FontFace token, one
 --font-sans source (v0.55.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes #4. A brand may now embed a webfont instead of relying on the
system stack: `fontFaces: [{ family, src: data:font/…;base64, weight,
style, display }]` in brand.json. Each face is emitted as a self-contained
`@font-face` rule (data: URI src + format() hint, font-display: swap by
default) in the generated style.css — no CDN, no cross-origin fetch,
CSP-clean — and its family leads the stack; the brand's `font` string
(the zero-load system stack by default) stays the fallback tail.

font-family now has exactly ONE source: the typed FontFamily token
(font.ts) derived by deriveFontFamily() in derive.ts, which both emitters
consume — to-css.ts as the `--font-sans` :root token (a base CSSStyleValue
reified via its cssText, replacing the CSSKeywordValue misuse) and
to-tokens.ts as `fontFamily.sans` (DTCG, face metadata under
$extensions) / `font.family.sans` (Style Dictionary). audit.ts strips
@font-face blocks (they DEFINE a face) and now fails any `font-family`
that is not `var(--font-sans)`. Existing brands derive byte-identical CSS;
their token JSON gains the fontFamily entry.

- font.ts / gen-font.ts: FontFace, FontDisplay, FONT_FORMAT_BY_MIME,
  fontFormatOf (font.ts regenerated from the generator template)
- config.ts: `font` must end in a generic family; new `fontFaces`
- brands/webfont-demo + examples/mock-webfont: a fixture with a
  basic-Latin subset of Poppins Regular (SIL OFL 1.1) as a WOFF data URI,
  gated in tokens-check.yml alongside burnt-orange and deep-blue
- GROUNDING.md: CSS Fonts 4 §font-face-rule / §src-desc / §font-display

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
